From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:40:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Take font families as ids already looked up

`StyleProperty::FontFamilyIds`: the families of a `font-family` value as
`fontique::FamilyId`s, in order of preference. It sets what
`StyleProperty::FontFamily` does, and either replaces the other over a
range or in a span.

Resolving `FontFamily` looks every name of the list up in the collection
(a lowercased key and a hash lookup each), for every span that sets it. A
caller that styles many spans with the same few lists, as a CSS engine
does, can look a list up once, keep the ids and give them here: generic
families are ids too (`Collection::generic_families`). The ids have to be
of the collection the layout is built with; one that isn't there selects
no font, as a name that isn't there.

Tests: ids pick the fonts their names do, in the list's order; ids and
names replace each other over a range and in a tree builder's span; a
root with no families takes them from a span around its text; no ids are
an empty list.
---
 parley/src/resolve/mod.rs           |   2 +
 parley/src/style/mod.rs             |   6 +
 parley/src/tests/mod.rs             |   1 +
 parley/src/tests/test_family_ids.rs | 164 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 173 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 parley/src/tests/test_family_ids.rs

diff --git a/parley/src/resolve/mod.rs b/parley/src/resolve/mod.rs
